<details class="cap-mobnav"><summary><span>OSAT Services</span><span class="cap-mobnav-meta">11<span class="cap-mobnav-chev"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></span></summary><div class="cap-mobnav-list"><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Design</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/package-design" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Package Design &amp; Simulation</a><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Packaging solutions</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/power-packages" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Power Packages — SiC &amp; GaN</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/qfn-dfn-lga" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>QFN, DFN &amp; LGA</a><a aria-current="page" href="/capabilities/osat/optical-packaging" class="cap-sub-leaf cap-active"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Clear &amp; Optical Packaging</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/hermetic-ceramic" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Hermetic &amp; Ceramic Packaging</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/ultra-small-packages" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Ultra-small Packages</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/system-in-package" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>System in Package (SiP)</a><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Wafer, assembly &amp; test</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-processing" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Processing</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-level-packaging" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Level Packaging</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/flip-chip" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Flip Chip &amp; Interconnect</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-probe-final-test" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Probe &amp; Final Test</a><span class="cap-sub-leaf cap-removed"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Die Attach &amp; Wire Bond</span></div></details>
<div class="sc-hero-band" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:#fff;position:relative;z-index:1;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band cap-section--hero"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;">
    <div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:14px;">OSAT · Clear &amp; Optical Packaging</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:46px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin:0 0 18px;max-width:740px;text-wrap:balance;">Clear &amp; Optical Packaging</h1>
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:18px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 32px;text-wrap:pretty;">Optical packaging has a direct role in controlling the light path, filtering unwanted wavelengths, and achieving the required package dimensions.</p>
    <div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);width:100%;height:407px;"><img src="/images/photos/cap-osat-optical-packaging-hero.webp" alt="Clear-molded optical sensor packages with visible windows, dies and wire bonds" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center;" /></div>
    <div class="hana-spec-block" style="margin-top:18px;"><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Ultrathin optical LGA, in production</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">0.30 mm</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Optical QFN working temperature</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">125 °C</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Footprint, one package generation</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">−25%</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Moisture sensitivity level reached</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">MSL1</div></div></div>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="sc-pillars-band" data-hana-bg="wafer" data-variant="light" data-accent="" data-fade="none" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f5f7fa 35%,#d8e6f3 100%);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Capability overview</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">The package must control the optical path while meeting thickness, footprint, and assembly requirements.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-3"><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="sun" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Clear mold &amp; optics</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">The optical path is engineered into the package itself.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Clear transfer molding over the optical die</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Custom caps and filters matched to the device</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Wavelength-selective filtering to reject interference</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Metal or plastic caps, ink masks, and film-assist molding</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="minimize-2" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Thin and small</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">For wearables and compact sensors, package thickness and footprint are often the limiting constraints.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Wafer backgrind to 3 mils for ultra-thin builds</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Progressive package-thickness reduction across three generations</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Stacked emitter-over-detector architecture to reduce footprint</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Footprints as small as 1 × 1.5 mm</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="thermometer" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Environment</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Built for the thermal and reflow conditions the finished sensor will see.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Operating temperatures up to 100 °C and 125 °C</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">High-temperature clear molding compounds</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Opto-couplers in DIP, SOIC, and SO packages</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Qualification against the customer's reflow profile</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:44px;"><div class="why-grid"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#155F9B 0%,#0E4A7C 46%,#0A3860 100%);border:none;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark-white.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.24);"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">MSL1 simplifies moisture-sensitive handling</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.84);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Moisture-sensitive plastic packages normally require dry packing, controlled floor life, and rebaking if that window expires. At MSL1, those handling constraints are removed.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">No pre-solder bake required</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">No dry-pack or desiccant handling</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">No floor-life countdown after opening</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Improved from MSL3 to MSL1 on the same package</span></li></ul></div><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#FFFFFF 0%,#E5EEF5 58%,#D8E6F1 100%);border:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:#BFD4E4;"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Package construction can be adapted to the device requirements</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Hana develops the package construction in-house, allowing body dimensions, die stack, and footprint to be adapted as device requirements evolve.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Package construction engineered in-house</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Thinner package bodies without redesigning the die</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Each package generation qualified before further reduction</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;border-bottom:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Standard footprints retained whenever they meet the requirement</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Where we run it</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Clear and optical packaging is available across our OSAT network; production mix varies by site.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-4"><a href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">Thailand</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Ayutthaya</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Ayutthaya <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">China</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Jiaxing</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Jiaxing <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;"><details class="sc-faq" open><summary>Can you mold a clear package over an optical sensor?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes — clear transfer mold, with a cap or filter designed to control the optical path and reject the wavelengths the device does not want. The cap can be metal or plastic, or replaced by an ink mask where the body has to stay thin.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>How thin can an optical package be?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">0.30 mm in production, as an optical LGA built on die ground to 3 mils. That is the thinnest package Hana builds in any family, optical or not.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Do you design the cap and filter, or do we supply the design?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">We design them. The cap or filter is drawn to the device and to the wavelengths it needs to reject — see <a href="/capabilities/osat/package-design" style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:600;">Package design &amp; simulation</a> for how that runs before tooling is cut.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Do you thin the wafer, or do we supply thinned die?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Either. Backgrind and singulation run in-house on the same OSAT operation, so a full-thickness wafer can come straight in — see <a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-processing" style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:600;">Wafer processing</a>.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What limits how thin an optical package can go?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">The die must be ground thin enough to fit while remaining suitable for handling, and the clear compound above it must maintain the optical path. Each reduction in package thickness requires qualification of the revised construction.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What happens if no standard optical body fits?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">We can design one — leadframe, outline and footprint, with thermal and warpage simulation before tooling is cut. If a standard footprint already fits, we build to that instead.</div></details></div></div></div></div>
